# Compose stack configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` IN THIS DIRECTORY:
#
#   cp infra/docker/.env.example infra/docker/.env
#
# Compose resolves its env file against the project directory — the directory
# holding the first `-f` file — not the shell's working directory. A `.env` at
# the repository root is not read by this stack, however the command is invoked.
#
# Only the `full` profile needs any of this. `pnpm docker:up` brings up postgres
# and redis alone and requires no env file at all.
#
# Never commit a populated `.env`.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ secrets
# Generate each with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64'))"
#
# Both must be at least 32 characters and MUST differ from each other — the api
# container runs with NODE_ENV=production and refuses to boot otherwise, exiting
# with a report that names the offending variable.
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=
